{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI-Assisted Pull Request Review.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI-Assisted Pull Request Review.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ai assisted pull request review ai assisted pull request review","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/AI-Assisted Pull Request Review.md","fileName":"AI-Assisted Pull Request Review.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"AI-Assisted Pull Request Review","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI-Assisted DevOps Practice]]","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI-Assisted Pull Request Review.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI-Assisted Pull Request Review.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ai assisted pull request review ai assisted pull request review","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/AI-Assisted Pull Request Review.md","fileName":"AI-Assisted Pull Request Review.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"AI-Assisted Pull Request Review","heading":"AI-Assisted Pull Request Review","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"AI can support a [[Pull Request]] by summarizing changes, explaining failed tests, suggesting missing coverage, and surfacing risky areas. These outputs increase reviewer visibility, especially when they are combined with deterministic gates for builds, formatting, dependencies, and test coverage.\n\nThe model should not approve its own work, ignore a failing check, or infer changes that are absent from the available evidence. Release confidence comes from a better-informed human decision, not from replacing review with an automated opinion. The pull request remains the auditable boundary where evidence, discussion, and approval meet.","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Fu